1
00:00:01,230 --> 00:00:05,230
Welcome to the Build America, Buy America Act training series.

2
00:00:05,230 --> 00:00:14,230
Before continuing, please watch the other videos within our training series on FEMA's Buy America website to ensure you have the essential background knowledge.

3
00:00:14,230 --> 00:00:22,230
As those training videos explain, the Build America, Buy America Act mandates that federal agencies, including FEMA,

4
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:29,230
ensure that all materials used in infrastructure projects funded by federal financial assistance are made in the U.S.

5
00:00:29,230 --> 00:00:35,230
But remember, FEMA's disaster financial assistance grants are exempt from these requirements.

6
00:00:35,230 --> 00:00:42,230
The Build America, Buy America Act grants FEMA the authority to waive the requirements under certain circumstances.

7
00:00:42,230 --> 00:00:51,230
As you previously learned, there are two categories of waivers, project-specific waivers, which apply to one specific infrastructure project,

8
00:00:51,230 --> 00:00:56,230
and general applicability waivers, which can be applied more broadly.

9
00:00:56,230 --> 00:01:02,230
This video will discuss FEMA's general applicability waivers by answering the following questions.

10
00:01:02,230 --> 00:01:05,230
What is a general applicability waiver?

11
00:01:05,230 --> 00:01:09,230
What general applicability waivers has FEMA issued?

12
00:01:09,230 --> 00:01:15,230
Do recipients or subrecipients need to apply to use a FEMA-approved general applicability waiver?

13
00:01:15,230 --> 00:01:20,230
Where can you find more information about the Build America, Buy America Act?

14
00:01:20,230 --> 00:01:22,230
Let's start with the first question.

15
00:01:22,230 --> 00:01:25,230
What is a general applicability waiver?

16
00:01:25,230 --> 00:01:33,230
The term general applicability waiver refers to a waiver that applies across multiple agency projects or awards.

17
00:01:33,230 --> 00:01:38,230
They are targeted to either a specific product or category of products,

18
00:01:38,230 --> 00:01:44,230
or to all products under the covered projects or awards, and always have an expiration date.

19
00:01:44,230 --> 00:01:47,230
Now, let's discuss the second question.

20
00:01:47,230 --> 00:01:51,230
What general applicability waivers has FEMA issued?

21
00:01:51,230 --> 00:01:56,230
FEMA has issued several general applicability waivers to ease the burden of compliance

22
00:01:56,230 --> 00:02:00,230
for its recipients and subrecipients as appropriate.

23
00:02:00,230 --> 00:02:07,230
The full list of FEMA's general applicability waivers can be found on FEMA's Buy America website at FEMA.gov.

24
00:02:07,230 --> 00:02:13,230
This video will cover the waivers most likely to be used by recipients and subrecipients.

25
00:02:13,230 --> 00:02:17,230
Small projects waiver and de minimis waiver.

26
00:02:17,230 --> 00:02:24,230
The small projects general applicability waiver allows FEMA to waive the Build America, Buy America Act requirements for projects

27
00:02:24,230 --> 00:02:30,230
where the total project costs do not exceed the current federal simplified acquisition threshold.

28
00:02:30,230 --> 00:02:37,230
The total project costs includes all funding applied toward the infrastructure project, regardless of source.

29
00:02:37,230 --> 00:02:41,230
When using the small projects general applicability waiver,

30
00:02:41,230 --> 00:02:45,230
recipients must maintain documentation showing that the total project costs

31
00:02:45,230 --> 00:02:51,230
are less than the current federal simplified acquisition threshold for the life of the award.

32
00:02:51,230 --> 00:02:55,230
If there are unplanned cost overruns that increase the project cost,

33
00:02:55,230 --> 00:03:00,230
all excess costs and additional purchases over the current federal simplified acquisition threshold

34
00:03:00,230 --> 00:03:06,230
must comply with the Build America, Buy America Act, unless otherwise waived.

35
00:03:06,230 --> 00:03:08,230
Let's look at a quick example.

36
00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:15,230
A city plans to renovate a fire station and the total project cost comes to $200,000.

37
00:03:15,230 --> 00:03:19,230
The project includes funding from one of the FEMA grant programs,

38
00:03:19,230 --> 00:03:25,230
subject to the Build America, Buy America Act, in the amount of $150,000,

39
00:03:25,230 --> 00:03:29,230
with the other $50,000 coming from bonds sold by the city.

40
00:03:29,230 --> 00:03:35,230
Since the total project cost is less than the current federal simplified acquisition threshold,

41
00:03:35,230 --> 00:03:40,230
the project qualifies for FEMA's small project general applicability waiver.

42
00:03:40,230 --> 00:03:47,230
It is important to know that while the Build America, Buy America Act requirements are waived for small projects,

43
00:03:47,230 --> 00:03:54,230
all recipients are encouraged to purchase items produced in the United States to the greatest extent practicable.

44
00:03:54,230 --> 00:03:59,230
The next FEMA waiver we will cover is the de minimis general applicability waiver.

45
00:03:59,230 --> 00:04:07,230
This waiver waives the requirements for up to 5% of the total material costs subject to the Build America, Buy America Act,

46
00:04:07,230 --> 00:04:10,230
with a maximum limit of $1 million.

47
00:04:10,230 --> 00:04:17,230
Recipients and sub-recipients that use this waiver must maintain documentation demonstrating compliance.

48
00:04:17,230 --> 00:04:21,230
This includes tracking the costs of products claimed under the waiver,

49
00:04:21,230 --> 00:04:25,230
as well as the total applicable project costs.

50
00:04:25,230 --> 00:04:30,230
Let's consider this example of using the de minimis general applicability waiver.

51
00:04:30,230 --> 00:04:36,230
A city plans to construct a new emergency operation center with a total cost of $20 million.

52
00:04:36,230 --> 00:04:42,230
The project includes $10 million in labor costs and $10 million in total material costs,

53
00:04:42,230 --> 00:04:46,230
subject to the Build America, Buy America Act.

54
00:04:46,230 --> 00:04:49,230
The project would be eligible to apply the de minimis waiver

55
00:04:49,230 --> 00:04:56,230
towards $500,000 worth of material costs, which represents 5% of the total $10 million

56
00:04:56,230 --> 00:05:01,230
in total material costs subject to the Build America, Buy America Act.

57
00:05:01,230 --> 00:05:04,230
Now let's discuss the third question.

58
00:05:04,230 --> 00:05:11,230
Do recipients or sub-recipients need to apply to use a FEMA approved general applicability waiver?

59
00:05:11,230 --> 00:05:16,230
No, there was no application process to use the general applicability waivers

60
00:05:16,230 --> 00:05:20,230
that FEMA has issued and listed on FEMA.gov.

61
00:05:20,230 --> 00:05:26,230
Any projects that are funded by a FEMA grant program, subject to the Build America, Buy America Act,

62
00:05:26,230 --> 00:05:30,230
can use a relevant FEMA approved general applicability waiver.

63
00:05:30,230 --> 00:05:35,230
As a best practice, recipients and sub-recipients who use these waivers

64
00:05:35,230 --> 00:05:39,230
are encouraged to maintain proper documentation of their use,

65
00:05:39,230 --> 00:05:43,230
as these waivers do expire and are not guaranteed to be renewed.

66
00:05:43,230 --> 00:05:46,230
Now let's discuss the last question.

67
00:05:46,230 --> 00:05:51,230
Where can I find more information on the Build America, Buy America Act?

68
00:05:51,230 --> 00:05:58,230
You can find information on FEMA's implementation of the Build America, Buy America Act on their website,

69
00:05:58,230 --> 00:06:02,230
located under the Buy America preference tab on FEMA.gov.

70
00:06:02,230 --> 00:06:07,230
This website includes a list of all FEMA grant programs subject to

71
00:06:07,230 --> 00:06:11,230
and not subject to the Build America, Buy America Act.

72
00:06:11,230 --> 00:06:17,230
You can also find more program definitions, flyers, and a helpful decision roadmap.

73
00:06:17,230 --> 00:06:21,230
The Code of Federal Regulations website provides more information

74
00:06:21,230 --> 00:06:27,230
on the Build America, Buy America Act policy under to CFR Part 184.

75
00:06:27,230 --> 00:06:32,230
Thank you for watching this video on FEMA's general applicability waivers.

76
00:06:32,230 --> 00:06:35,230
To continue learning about the Build America, Buy America Act,

77
00:06:35,230 --> 00:06:39,230
be sure to check out the other videos in this training series.

78
00:06:39,230 --> 00:06:44,230
For more information, please visit FEMA's Buy America website on FEMA.gov

79
00:06:44,230 --> 00:06:55,230
or contact us at FEMA-grants-buyamerica.fema.dhs.gov.

